+# Running the native tests without Xcode
+
+`Package.swift` at the project root is a Swift Package Manager harness. It
+compiles the **real** `Models.swift`, `Scheduling.swift`, `DinnerCatalog.swift`
+and `SessionStore.swift` (no copies) together with the **real**
+`DinnerTogetherTests/DinnerTogetherTests.swift`, and runs all 60 XCTest
+methods in 12 classes. That is actual Swift execution of the engine and the
+store — a step the JavaScript model cannot provide.
+
+What it does not cover: the SwiftUI views (`CookingView`, `Sheets`,
+`PlanView`, `ContentView`, `Theme`), `TimerCenter`, and the real
+`NotificationManager` (UserNotifications). Those still need Xcode and a
+device or simulator.
+
+## Run it
+
+macOS with Xcode 16 command-line tools (or any Swift 6.0+ toolchain):
+
+```
+cd DinnerTogether-RecoveryCandidate-v028
+swift test
+swift test --filter RecoveryNoticeTests     # one class
+swift test --filter RecoveryStoreTests
+```
+
+Linux, or any machine with Docker:
+
+```
+cd DinnerTogether-RecoveryCandidate-v028
+docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/src -w /src swift:6.0 swift test
+```
+
+A `.build/` directory appears next to the project; delete it freely. Keep
+opening `DinnerTogether.xcodeproj` as before — Xcode ignores `Package.swift`.
+
+## How it stays honest
+
+- No source is duplicated. The package's `sources:` list points at the app's
+  own files, so what runs is what ships.
+- `DinnerTogether/EngineTestSupport.swift` replaces `Notifications.swift`
+  inside the harness only: the `NotificationService` protocol is copied
+  verbatim and `NotificationManager` is inert. Every test injects
+  `MockNotifications`, so the real manager is never constructed in tests on
+  any platform. **Do not add this file to the Xcode target** (it would
+  collide with `Notifications.swift`).
+- On Linux only, `EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim` provides a module named
+  `SwiftUI` containing just `ObservableObject` and `@Published`, so
+  `SessionStore.swift`'s `import SwiftUI` resolves. On macOS the real
+  framework is used.
+
+## First-run watch items (written on Linux without a toolchain; unexecuted)
+
+1. **Swift 6.0+ required.** `SessionStore.init` uses `URL.documentsDirectory`
+   and `URL.appending(path:)`; on Linux these come from the Swift 6
+   Foundation. If an older toolchain reports them missing, use the
+   `swift:6.0` image.
+2. **`@MainActor` test classes on Linux.** swift-corelibs-xctest runs
+   `@MainActor`-isolated async tests in Swift 6; if a class fails to launch
+   rather than fail an assertion, report the toolchain version.
+3. **Target named `SwiftUI` (Linux only).** If SwiftPM refuses the module
+   name, rename the shim target and add `import SwiftUI`→shim mapping via
+   `-Xswiftc -module-alias SwiftUI=SwiftUIShim` instead. Not expected.
+4. **Timing-sensitive tests.** `testNoStaleReminderAfter*DuringPendingAuth`
+   and `testIndependentStartsKeepBothReminders` use real sleeps
+   (0.02–0.3 s); on a slow CI runner they could flake. They are the
+   baseline's tests, unchanged.
+5. **Locale.** `Scheduling.formatTime` uses the short time style; the tests
+   only check step titles and phrases ("late to start", "check the food"),
+   never formatted times, so locale differences shouldn't matter.
+
+Record the toolchain (`swift --version`), platform, and the per-class pass
+or fail list in `RECOVERY_HANDOFF.md` §3 when this has run.
diff -ruN -x '*.patch' -x .build a/EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim/SwiftUI.swift b/EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim/SwiftUI.swift
--- a/EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim/SwiftUI.swift	1969-12-31 17:00:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim/SwiftUI.swift	2026-10-09 15:07:44.928929805 -0600
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+// Linux-only stand-in module named `SwiftUI`, used by Package.swift so that
+// SessionStore.swift's `import SwiftUI` resolves where SwiftUI/Combine don't
+// exist. It provides only the two things the store uses from that import:
+// the ObservableObject marker protocol and the @Published property wrapper.
+// No observation happens; the harness tests read state directly.
+//
+// Never compiled on macOS or iOS (Package.swift adds this target only on
+// Linux), so it cannot shadow the real framework there.
+
+public protocol ObservableObject: AnyObject {}
+
+@propertyWrapper
+public struct Published<Value> {
+    public var wrappedValue: Value
+    public init(wrappedValue: Value) { self.wrappedValue = wrappedValue }
+    public init(initialValue: Value) { self.wrappedValue = initialValue }
+}
diff -ruN -x '*.patch' -x .build a/Package.swift b/Package.swift
--- a/Package.swift	1969-12-31 17:00:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/Package.swift	2026-10-09 15:07:28.132928807 -0600
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+// swift-tools-version:5.9
+//
+// Engine + store test harness — lets `swift test` run the real scheduling
+// engine, the session store, and the canonical XCTest file WITHOUT Xcode:
+//
+//   macOS (Xcode 16 command-line tools or later):  swift test
+//   Linux / Docker:  docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/src -w /src swift:6.0 swift test
+//
+// This does not replace the Xcode project. Keep opening
+// DinnerTogether.xcodeproj as before; Xcode ignores this file. What the
+// harness compiles is exactly the app's Models.swift, Scheduling.swift,
+// DinnerCatalog.swift and SessionStore.swift (no copies), plus
+// DinnerTogetherTests/DinnerTogetherTests.swift. The SwiftUI views,
+// TimerCenter and the UserNotifications-backed NotificationManager are not
+// compiled here; they stay Xcode-only. See ENGINE_TESTS.md.
+//
+// Written on Linux without a Swift toolchain available — see ENGINE_TESTS.md
+// for the specific things to check the first time it runs.
+import PackageDescription
+
+#if os(Linux)
+// SessionStore.swift says `import SwiftUI` for ObservableObject/@Published.
+// On Linux a two-type stand-in module provides just those.
+let shimTargets: [Target] = [
+    .target(name: "SwiftUI", path: "EngineSupport/SwiftUIShim"),
+]
+let engineDependencies: [Target.Dependency] = ["SwiftUI"]
+#else
+let shimTargets: [Target] = []
+let engineDependencies: [Target.Dependency] = []
+#endif
+
+let package = Package(
+    name: "DinnerTogetherEngine",
+    platforms: [.macOS(.v13), .iOS(.v17)],
+    targets: shimTargets + [
+        .target(
+            name: "DinnerTogether",
+            dependencies: engineDependencies,
+            path: "DinnerTogether",
+            // Explicit list: only the engine and store, never the views.
+            // EngineTestSupport.swift stands in for Notifications.swift
+            // (protocol copied verbatim; inert manager). It is NOT in the
+            // Xcode target.
+            sources: [
+                "Models.swift",
+                "Scheduling.swift",
+                "DinnerCatalog.swift",
+                "SessionStore.swift",
+                "EngineTestSupport.swift",
+            ]
+        ),
+        .testTarget(
+            name: "DinnerTogetherTests",
+            dependencies: ["DinnerTogether"],
+            path: "DinnerTogetherTests"
+        ),
+    ]
+)
